  "dialogue": [
    {
      "turn_id": 0,
      "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
      "text": "Good afternoon, private banking, Rachel Tan speaking. How may I help you?"
    },
    {
      "turn_id": 1,
      "speaker": "CLIENT",
      "text": "Hello, Rachel, Daniel Lim here. 我现在在办公室，手边有投资记录，想趁工作空档跟您谈谈。 我的身份证号码是G五一二六六一七B。 My date of birth is 28 May 1955."
    },
    {
      "turn_id": 2,
      "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
      "text": "Thank you, Daniel. We can keep the discussion concise. Before we turn to your notes, are telephone appointments still convenient for your routine portfolio reviews?"
    },
    {
      "turn_id": 3,
      "speaker": "CLIENT",
      "text": "Phone calls are still best, but please arrange them by email rather than calling unexpectedly. 最近公司的配送安排常有变动，我经常要临时跟仓库和同事协调。收到预约邮件，我就能找个安静的地方谈，不用边走边接电话。"
    },
    {
      "turn_id": 4,
      "speaker": "EMPLOYEE",
      "text": "For routine reviews, I can contact you by email to arrange a convenient time. Let me confirm your investment objective: you want to free up liquidity for anticipated personal expenses while retaining some equity exposure."
    },
    {
      "turn_id": 5,
      "speaker": "CLIENT",
      "text": "Let me get the relevant page in front of me. 我的文件夹里还夹着之前做的比较笔记，您先按顺序讲，我边听边找对应的位置。今天桌上的文件有点多。"
    },
    {
